From: CARGT <engineering@cargt.com>
Subject: [PATCH] stm32mp25: enable env-based bootcount for A/B rollback safety

Closes the RAUC A/B rollback-safety gap documented in
docs/rauc-ota-updates.md section 2.5: previously, a bank committed via
set-primary that never reached a good boot would never automatically
fall back to the previous good bank - there was no countdown or retry
logic, only a one-way, persistent bootcmd rewrite.

CONFIG_FWU_MULTI_BANK_UPDATE was already enabled in this defconfig, and
U-Boot's generic autoboot logic (common/autoboot.c bootdelay_process())
consults it ahead of the plain bootcount mechanism whenever enabled -
but stm32mp2 has no fwu_plat_get_bootidx() implementation (unlike
stm32mp1, which reads a TAMP backup register also written by TF-A), so
it falls through to a weak default that reads the FWU metadata's
active_index directly and uses it as a boolean "run altbootcmd instead
of bootcmd" flag. Confirmed empirically on hardware (distinct marker
commands in bootcmd/altbootcmd, a full reset with autoboot left
uninterrupted): this weak default reliably resolves to "always run
bootcmd" regardless of active_index in our environment - i.e. it
currently provides no real A/B awareness at all, and disabling it costs
no working behavior.

Disables CONFIG_FWU_MULTI_BANK_UPDATE (CONFIG_FWU_MDATA_V2, the
metadata *format* our own update_metadata.sh/mkfwumdata tooling
depends on, is untouched - this only concerns the autoboot decision
path) so bootdelay_process() falls through to the standard
bootcount_error() check instead, and enables the generic, portable
env-based bootcount backend:
- CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT + CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ENV: no hardware register
  needed, bootcount/bootlimit tracked entirely in the persisted
  environment (drivers/bootcount/bootcount_env.c).
- CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_BOOTLIMIT=3: three real attempts at bootcmd before
  U-Boot's own generic autoboot logic automatically runs altbootcmd
  instead - matching the same 4-attempt convention TF-A's own
  (independent, firmware-level) FWU_MAX_TRIAL_REBOOT counter already
  uses.
- upgrade_available/bootcount default to 0 in the built-in environment:
  per drivers/bootcount/bootcount_env.c, bootcount only accumulates (and
  is only ever compared against bootlimit) while upgrade_available=1,
  so this is a safe no-op until something (st-boot-script.sh's
  set-primary, in a later commit) explicitly arms it for a new trial.

Upstream-Status: Pending [not sent upstream to ST - specific to this
board's RAUC A/B rollback design]

--- a/configs/stm32mp25_defconfig
+++ b/configs/stm32mp25_defconfig
@@ -26,6 +26,9 @@
 CONFIG_DISTRO_DEFAULTS=y
 CONFIG_BOOTDELAY=1
 CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND="echo 'Boot A';setenv altboot 0;run bootcmd_stm32mp"
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ENV=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_BOOTLIMIT=3
 CONFIG_FDT_SIMPLEFB=y
 CONFIG_SYS_PROMPT="STM32MP> "
 CONFIG_CMD_BDINFO_EXTRA=y
@@ -191,7 +194,7 @@
 # CONFIG_LMB_USE_MAX_REGIONS is not set
 CONFIG_LMB_MEMORY_REGIONS=2
 CONFIG_LMB_RESERVED_REGIONS=32
-CONFIG_FWU_MULTI_BANK_UPDATE=y
+# CONFIG_FWU_MULTI_BANK_UPDATE is not set
 CONFIG_FWU_MDATA_V2=y
 # CONFIG_TOOLS_MKEFICAPSULE is not set
 # CONFIG_TOOLS_MKFWUMDATA is not set
--- a/include/configs/stm32mp25_common.h
+++ b/include/configs/stm32mp25_common.h
@@ -93,6 +93,8 @@
 #define STM32MP_EXTRA \
 	"env_check=if env info -p -d -q; then env save; fi\0" \
 	"altbootcmd=echo 'Boot B';setenv altboot 1;run bootcmd_stm32mp\0" \
+	"upgrade_available=0\0" \
+	"bootcount=0\0" \
 	"boot_net_usb_start=true\0"
 /*
  * memory layout for 96MB uncompressed/compressed kernel,
